# Datsun Cherry 120A Coupe (F-II), 1977-1979.
#
# The F10 three-door liftback coupe, sold in Britain from 1977 and only with
# the 1,171 cc engine; the saloons were the 988 cc Cherry 100A and are not
# represented. The coupe carries the flat beltline, the full-length liftback
# tailgate and the large rectangular rear quarter glass.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Cherry
#
# Dimensions 3.825 x 1.500 x 1.375 m, wheelbase 2.395 m (Wikipedia infobox;
# the height is the range figure and may be a few centimetres high for the
# coupe, no coupe-specific height having been found).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the only true level side elevation of an F10
# coupe found, a period film photograph at 1282 x 770, so resolution rather
# than file size is its limit. Images 2-4 are a UK-registered 120A, APJ 364T.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour page for the F10 was obtained. White, Red,
# Blue and Green are plain names. The surviving UK 1977 car is described by its
# auctioneer as Polar White, Datsun code 216, but that is a lead, not a chart.
# Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 150 km/h. Comfort 40/390, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 40. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro 1977, the month unconfirmed and set to January; retire staggered
# 1990-1994 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-f10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-f10.dae. References:
# citycars/references/nissan-cherry-f10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the station picks from a period film photograph are
# approximate. The compound tail curves, the grille texture, the wheel centres
# and the badge lettering are simplified.


obj=citycar
